    75|<em>Diego: "Every footprint we leave is a promise to those who dared to dream before us."</em></p>
    76|<p>The regolith underfoot was finer than talc, sharper than shattered glass—a reminder that the Moon had known no water, no wind, no erosion for billions of years. Each step kicked up a plume of dust that hung in the airless silence before settling back to the gray surface, leaving temporary footprints that would last longer than any monument on Earth.</p>
